RUBRIQUE1 = 'HYDRO';'FLUID';'CORIOLIS EFFECT'
NIVEAU = 1
AIDE1 = 'Sets the value of the Coriolis force coefficient, in cartesian coordinates. This coefficient, denoted FCOR in the code, should be equal to 2ω sin(l) where ω denotes the earth angular speed of rotation and l the latitude. ω = 7.2921 10-5 rad/s. The Coriolis force components are then: FU = FCOR ×V, FV = −FCOR ×U. When using the spherical coordinates, the Coriolis coefficient is automatically computed.'
/
